// PEAR 2: a self-recursive local binding (`letrec`) with a base case.
//
// `fact` names itself inside its own body. PEAR 2 lifts every member of the
// group to a module-level function whose environment is `null` -- a recursive
// binding may not capture, because its own closure value does not exist while
// its body is being emitted -- and the self reference inside the body therefore
// denotes the constant closure `{ @pear2.lam.*, null }`. LLVM folds that pair
// straight back into a direct call.
//
// The recursive call sits inside the else arm, so the result type is decided by
// the arm that does not recurse; the `call`/`comu` continuation is the ordinary
// CPS shape for using a result, not a special case of the recursion.
//
// fact(5) = 120, so the program exits 120 - 78 = 42 at every tier.
air 2.2 Main "letrec_factorial_main.pie";

def main() : i64 =
  mu~ %ret.
    letrec (fact = lam (n : i64) -> if (lt n 2 : i64) then
                                   <1 : i64 | %ret>
                                 else
                                   <fact | call · (sub n 1 : i64) · comu m.
                                     <(mul n m) | %ret>>) in
      <fact | call · 5 : i64 · comu f.
        <(sub f 78 : i64) | %ret>>;
